                    "text": "Agent: explore\nDescription: Find control loop and state machine\nDurationMs: 72802\nTotalTokens: 535K\n\nOutput:\nNow I have a complete picture. Here is a comprehensive trace of the **entire call chain** from control loop to enable command sending.\n\n---\n\n## Full Call Chain Analysis\n\n### 1. System Entry → Initialization\n\n**`Core/Src/main.c:69-121`** — The `main()` function:\n1. HAL and peripheral initialization\n2. `HAL_Delay(2000)` — 2-second power-on hold\n3. `Robot_Init()` — user initialization\n4. Empty `while(1)` loop — all work is timer-driven\n\n**`Development_Layer/Task/CallBack_Task/callback_task.cpp:14-26`** — `Robot_Init()`:\n```c\nCAN_Init(&hcan1, CAN1_Callback);   // CAN1 with RX callback\ndog.Chassis_Init();                 // Init 4 legs × 2 motors = 8 DM motors\nTIM_Init(&htim6, Tim6_Robot_1ms_Callback);  // Bind TIM6 IRQ\nHAL_TIM_Base_Start_IT(&htim6);     // Start 1ms periodic interrupt\ninit_finished = true;               // Enables CAN RX processing\n```\n\n### 2. Motor Initialization Chain\n\n**`Development_Layer/Function_Class/Class_RobotDog/robotdog_class.cpp:13-35`** — `CLASS_DOG::Chassis_Init()`:\nCreates 4 `Class_SingleDogFoot_DM` objects, each with 2 `Class_Motor_DM_Normal` instances:\n| Foot | Inner Motor (mi) CAN ID | Outer Motor (mo) CAN ID |\n|------|------------------------|------------------------|\n| Foot1_Left_Back | 0x012→0x002 | 0x011→0x001 |\n| Foot2_Right_Back | 0x013→0x003 | 0x014→0x004 |\n| Foot3_Left_Front | 0x017→0x007 | 0x018→0x008 |\n| Foot4_Right_Front | 0x016→0x006 | 0x015→0x005 |\n\n**`Development_Layer/Robot_Control/Foot_Control/foot_control.cpp:8-44`** — `SingleFoot_Init()`:\nEach motor gets `.Init()` → `Class_Motor_DM_Normal::Init()` at **`Motor_DM.cpp:40-84`** which:\n- Stores the CAN manage object pointer (CAN1 or CAN2)\n- Sets CAN_Rx_ID and CAN_Tx_ID (with control-method offset: MIT=+0x000, AngleOmega=+0x100, Omega=+0x200, EMIT=+0x300)\n- Default control method is `Motor_DM_Control_Method_NORMAL_MIT`\n- KP=2.0, KD=0.01 are set\n\n**CRITICAL: Lines 39-40 in foot_control.cpp are COMMENTED OUT:**\n```c\n// mo.CAN_Send_Enter();\n// mi.CAN_Send_Enter();\n```\nMotors are **NOT explicitly enabled** during init. Enable happens reactively in the control loop.\n\n### 3. The Main Control Loop (1ms Timer ISR)\n\n**`Development_Layer/Task/CallBack_Task/callback_task.cpp:29-57`** — `Tim6_Robot_1ms_Callback()`:\n\nThis is the **heart of the entire system**. Called every 1ms by TIM6 interrupt:\n```\nTIM6 IRQ → HAL_TIM_PeriodElapsedCallback() → TIM6_Manage_Object.Callback_Function() → Tim6_Robot_1ms_Callback()\n```\n(Dispatched via `Development_Layer/Driver/Tim/drv_tim.cpp:93-175`)\n\nThe callback:\n1. Sets `robot_1ms_cycle_flag = true`\n2. Counts to derive 100ms and 1000ms flags (both declared as `volatile bool` globals in `robotdog_class.cpp:9-11`)\n3. **Sets foot target position**: `dog.Foot1_Left_Back.Set_x_y(0.01, 0.06)` — currently only Foot1 has a non-zero target\n4. **Calls the main control**: `dog.Chassis_Control()`\n\n### 4. Chassis Control → Per-Foot Control\n\n**`robotdog_class.cpp:50-60`** — `CLASS_DOG::Chassis_Control()`:\nCalls `Foot_control()` on all 4 feet sequentially.\n\n**`foot_control.cpp:98-118`** — `Class_SingleDogFoot_DM::Foot_control()`:\n```\nFoot_control()\n  ├── FootXY_map_MotorAngle()     ← Inverse kinematics: (X,Y) → motor angles\n  │     Uses law of cosines with Long_L=0.1275, Short_L=0.085\n  │     Applies Left/Right side mirroring\n  │     Calls mi.Set_Control_Angle() and mo.Set_Control_Angle()\n  │     Returns HAL_ERROR if out of bounds (±Low_limit/High_limit)\n  │\n  └── mi.Dog_Send_Callback()      ← Send command to inner motor\n  └── mo.Dog_Send_Callback()      ← Send command to outer motor\n```\n\n### 5. Enable/Auto-Enable Logic (The State Machine)\n\n**`Motor_DM.cpp:315-339`** — `Class_Motor_DM_Normal::Dog_Send_Callback()`:\n\nThis is the **state machine** for motor enable/disable:\n```c\nif (Rx_Data.Control_Status == Motor_DM_Control_Status_ENABLE)   // = 0x1\n    → Constrain values → Output() → CAN_Send_Data()  [normal control]\n\nelse if (Rx_Data.Control_Status == Motor_DM_Control_Status_DISABLE)  // = 0x0\n    → CAN_Send_Enter()   // AUTO-REENABLE\n\nelse  // any error state (overvoltage=0x8, undervoltage, overcurrent, overtemp, etc.)\n    → CAN_Send_Clear_Error()   // clear fault, then next cycle will re-enable\n```\n\nThe `Rx_Data.Control_Status` comes from the **DM motor's own CAN feedback** — byte 0 bit[7:4] of the DM motor's status message, parsed in `Data_Process()` at line 364:\n```c\nRx_Data.Control_Status = static_cast<Enum_Motor_DM_Control_Status_Normal>(tmp_buffer->Control_Status_Enum);\n```\n\n**The first time a motor sends back status, it will be DISABLE (0x0), so `CAN_Send_Enter()` fires** — this is the implicit enable mechanism.\n\n### 6. CAN Send Path\n\n**`Motor_DM.cpp:401-464`** — `Class_Motor_DM_Normal::Output()`:\nPacks control values into a `Tx_Data[8]` buffer per the control mode (MIT, Angle_Omega, Omega, EMIT), then calls:\n```c\nCAN_Send_Data(CAN_Manage_Object->CAN_Handler, CAN_Tx_ID, Tx_Data, 8);\n```\n\n**`drv_can.cpp:168-200`** — `CAN_Send_Data()`:\n```c\ndo {\n    send_status = HAL_CAN_AddTxMessage(hcan, &TxHeader, Data, &tx_mailbox);\n    if (send_status != HAL_OK) {\n        for (volatile uint32_t i = 0U; i < 500U; i++) { }  // ~111μs delay\n        retry_cnt--;\n    }\n} while ((send_status != HAL_OK) && (retry_cnt > 0U));\n```\nRetries up to 200 times (~2ms total). Updates TX statistics on completion.\n\n### 7. The \"Alive Check\" Mechanism (Currently UNUSED)\n\n**`Motor_DM.cpp:264-279`** — `RTOS_100ms_Alive_Callback()`:\n```c\nif (Flag == Pre_Flag) {\n    Motor_DM_Status = Motor_DM_Status_DISABLE;   // motor disconnected\n} else {\n    Motor_DM_Status = Motor_DM_Status_ENABLE;    // motor alive\n}\nPre_Flag = Flag;\n```\n- `Flag` is incremented by `CAN_RxCpltCallback()` (line 220) every time a CAN message is received from the motor\n- If no message arrives for 100ms, `Flag == Pre_Flag` → status = DISABLE\n\n**IMPORTANT: `RTOS_100ms_Alive_Callback()` is NEVER CALLED in the current codebase.** There is no timer or task that invokes it. Similarly, `RTOS_Send_Callback()` (line 285, which also sends enter/enable commands) is never called. Only `Dog_Send_Callback()` is actually invoked (from `Foot_control()`). There is also no \"heartbeat\" named function — the alive check uses a sliding window flag comparison.\n\n### 8. CAN RX Path (Feedback)\n\n**`drv_can.cpp:297-321`** — `HAL_CAN_RxFifo0Callback()`:\n- Triggered by hardware CAN RX interrupt\n- Reads message into `manager_obj->Rx_Buffer`\n- Checks `init_finished` guard\n- Calls registered callback: `CAN1_Callback()`\n\n**`callback_task.cpp:64-105`** — `CAN1_Callback()`:\n- Matches `StdId` against each motor's `Get_CAN_Rx_ID()`\n- Calls `mi.CAN_RxCpltCallback(Rx_Data)` or `mo.CAN_RxCpltCallback(Rx_Data)`\n\n**`Motor_DM.cpp:216-222`** — `CAN_RxCpltCallback()`:\n- Increments `Flag` (alive check counter)\n- Calls `Data_Process()` which parses angle/omega/torque/temperatures and `Control_Status`\n\n---\n\n## Summary Diagram\n\n```\nmain()  [Core/Src/main.c]\n  └─ Robot_Init()  [callback_task.cpp:14]\n       ├─ CAN_Init(&hcan1, CAN1_Callback)  [drv_can.cpp:106]\n       ├─ dog.Chassis_Init()  [robotdog_class.cpp:13]\n       │    └─ SingleFoot_Init() × 4  [foot_control.cpp:8]\n       │         └─ mo.Init() / mi.Init()  [Motor_DM.cpp:40]  (CAN_Send_Enter COMMENTED OUT)\n       ├─ TIM_Init(&htim6, Tim6_Robot_1ms_Callback)  [drv_tim.cpp:28]\n       └─ HAL_TIM_Base_Start_IT(&htim6)\n\nTIM6 IRQ (1ms)\n  └─ Tim6_Robot_1ms_Callback()  [callback_task.cpp:29]\n       ├─ Set_x_y(0.01, 0.06)  [only Foot1 gets non-zero target]\n       └─ dog.Chassis_Control()  [robotdog_class.cpp:50]\n            └─ Foot_control() × 4  [foot_control.cpp:98]\n                 ├─ FootXY_map_MotorAngle()  [IK: (X,Y)→motor angles]\n                 └─ mi.Dog_Send_Callback() / mo.Dog_Send_Callback()  [Motor_DM.cpp:315]\n                      ├─ If ENABLE  → Output() → CAN_Send_Data()  [drv_can.cpp:168]\n                      ├─ If DISABLE → CAN_Send_Enter()  [auto-re-enable]\n                      └─ If ERROR   → CAN_Send_Clear_Error()\n\nCAN RX IRQ\n  └─ CAN1_Callback()  [callback_task.cpp:64]\n       └─ mi.CAN_RxCpltCallback() / mo.CAN_RxCpltCallback()  [Motor_DM.cpp:216]\n            ├─ Flag++  (alive check counter)\n            └─ Data_Process()  [parses motor feedback + Control_Status]\n```\n\n### Key Files Reference\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `Core/Src/main.c` | Entry point, calls `Robot_Init()` |\n| `Development_Layer/Task/CallBack_Task/callback_task.cpp` | Main control loop (Tim6_Robot_1ms_Callback), CAN RX dispatch |\n| `Development_Layer/Function_Class/Class_RobotDog/robotdog_class.cpp` | Robot dog class: `Chassis_Init()`, `Chassis_Control()` |\n| `Development_Layer/Robot_Control/Foot_Control/foot_control.cpp` | Single leg: IK, per-foot `Foot_control()` |\n| `Development_Layer/External_Device/Motor/Motor_DM.cpp` | DM motor driver: enable/disable state machine, alive check, CAN output |\n| `Development_Layer/Driver/CAN/drv_can.cpp` | CAN send/receive/init, bus status, retry logic |\n| `Development_Layer/Driver/Tim/drv_tim.cpp` | Timer IRQ dispatch to registered callbacks |\n\n### Notable Gaps / Observations\n\n1. **No explicit motor enable on startup** — `CAN_Send_Enter()` calls in `SingleFoot_Init()` are commented out. Enable happens reactively in `Dog_Send_Callback()` when the motor reports DISABLE status.\n2. **Alive check (`RTOS_100ms_Alive_Callback`) exists but is never scheduled** — no timer or task calls it. The `Motor_DM_Status` variable (which it sets) is defined but never read in the current code path.\n3. **The `RTOS_Send_Callback()` is also uncalled** — only `Dog_Send_Callback()` runs.\n4. **Only Foot1 gets a non-zero target** — `Set_x_y(0.01, 0.06)` is only called for `Foot1_Left_Back`. All other feet get default X=Y=0